Now let me be careful about a few factual points:

1. "build script 运行时 cwd 是包根目录" — yes, Cargo runs build script with cwd = package root. cupti build.rs joins manifest_dir with csrc/... using CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR anyway. Fine.

2. stdout 非 cargo: 行为：Cargo book says "Build scripts may communicate... Any line printed to stdout of a build script that doesn't start with cargo: is hidden"... Actually: lines not starting with cargo: are shown only in verbose mode? Cargo docs: "any output on stdout that doesn't start with cargo: is only shown in verbose mode"? Hmm — actual behavior: build script stdout lines not prefixed with cargo: are displayed when running with -vv. Yes, that's documented ("stdout of the build script is only interpreted... other lines are ... shown in verbose"). I'll state it and have the experiment confirm.

3. rustc-link-lib default kind: dylib. ✓

4. link-search `native=`: "native" means host (non-Apple framework) library path; on Linux results in -L. ✓

5. rerun-if-changed with relative path: relative to package root? Cargo docs: paths are relative to the build script's package root? For `cargo:rerun-if-changed`, the doc says value is a path relative to the build script's package? Hmm: "cargo:rerun-if-changed=PATH — Tells Cargo to re-run the build script if the file at the given path has changed. ... PATH must be relative to the build script's package?" Actually docs say paths are relative to your package root... hmm, or cwd (which is package root). Same thing here since cwd is package root. I'll say 相对于包根目录（也是脚本的工作目录）.

6. Default rerun policy: "By default, Cargo will re-run the build script if any file in the package is changed." ✓ And with any rerun-if printed, default is overridden; changing build.rs itself still triggers rerun. ✓

